.TITLE "mdfind"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Finds files and directories on macOS using the Spotlight metadata index.
This command is significantly faster than traditional file system searches
(like `find` or `locate`) because it queries a pre-built index of file attributes.
It supports complex queries based on file names, content, creation dates, and more.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**findspotlight**

.DIV "TLDR"
**mdfind "__query__"**
Finds files matching a simple __query__ string.
> __query__: The search string.

**mdfind -name "__filename__"**
Finds files with a specific __filename__.
> __filename__: The name of the file to search for.

**mdfind -onlyin "__/path/to/directory__" "__query__"**
Searches for files matching __query__ only within a specified __/path/to/directory__.
> __/path/to/directory__: The directory to search within. | __query__: The search string.

**mdfind "kMDItemDisplayName == '*__pattern__*'"**
Finds files where the display name matches a __pattern__ using Spotlight query syntax.
> __pattern__: The glob pattern to match against the display name.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`mdfind` leverages the power of Spotlight, offering quick and efficient searches
across the entire system or specific locations. It's especially useful for
locating files when you know some metadata but not the exact path.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:open**

documentation: https://ss64.com/osx/mdfind.html
